From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Petr=20=C5=A0tetiar?= <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 07:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: take down and restore the partners of a driver owner
 interface
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

027 removes the BSSes of other interfaces that run on the driver of an
interface that is being removed or disabled, but only when that
interface's first BSS is a plain BSS. An interface whose first BSS is
itself an AP MLD link kept upstream's semantics: hostapd_cleanup_driver()
sees the driver shared with the partner links, removes only the departing
link and leaves the driver, its nl80211 context and the netdev to them.

On prplOS with pWHM that is the common topology. The MLD netdev is the
main VAP of the radio that came up first (wlan0.1), and the first BSSes
or secondary BSSes of the other radios are links of it that borrow its
context. When pWHM re-applies such a radio with a configuration in which
that VAP is no longer an AP MLD link, it sends REMOVE for the owner
interface and ADDs the new configuration, and the ADD initializes a new
driver on the same netdev while the surviving context still holds the
wdev's management frame registrations:

  hostapd: Remove interface 'wlan0.1_link0'
  hostapd: Configuration file: /tmp/wlan0_hapd.conf (phy wlan0) --> new PHY
  hostapd: nl80211: kernel reports: Match already configured
  hostapd: nl80211: Could not configure driver mode
  hostapd: nl80211 driver initialization failed.
  hostapd: Adding interface bss_config=wlan0 failed
  wld: wlan0: warm apply failed to add iface conf => restart to recover

cfg80211_mlme_register_mgmt() rejects a match that another socket has
already registered on the wdev with -EALREADY, and pWHM recovers with a
full hostapd restart. If instead the last partner link goes away later,
the driver stays allocated with drv->ctx pointing at a freed
hostapd_data and the next interface-down event on that netdev is
delivered to it.

Drop the AP MLD exclusion in hostapd_remove_drv_borrowers(): what
matters is that the driver behind bss[0] was created by this interface,
which hapd->drv_owner_iface records. The partners are taken down before
the driver cleanup, so that hostapd_cleanup_driver() finds the driver
unshared, deinitializes it and releases the netdev, and the ADD gets a
fresh driver.

The partners are not lost. Only an AP MLD link borrows a context itself
(hostapd_setup_bss() and driver_init(), both for an mld_ap BSS); a plain
secondary created through a borrowing first BSS records the same owner,
but its interface is disabled as a first-BSS partner before the
secondary walk gets to it. The owner may be an AP MLD link or a plain
BSS whose interface hosts the first links of other AP MLDs, as wlan2.1
does for the guest and backhaul MLDs once it has left the private MLD.
So the decision for a secondary partner is taken per partner, not per
owner:

- A partner that is the first BSS of its interface is disabled, keeping
  its configuration and control sockets. For an AP MLD owner it is
  also marked mld_partner_disabled.
- A partner that is a secondary BSS of a running interface and an AP
  MLD link is taken down like hostapd_remove_bss() does, but its
  configuration is parked on that interface, together with the
  identity the BSS had: its link ID (and so the control socket name
  <mld>_link<N>), its link address, its AP MLD (conf->iface and the
  MLD address), its order among the interface's BSSes and its radio
  (the interface's phy). Whether the owner is an AP MLD link or
  a plain BSS does not matter here.
- A plain partner, should one exist, is removed as 027 does.

When a later interface setup completes while such recovery is pending,
hostapd_mld_reattach_partners() runs from the event loop and restores
every partner whose own AP MLD has a running first BSS with a driver
again: a marked interface is enabled, and driver_init() borrows the new
context as before; a parked BSS is added back to its interface, in its
place among the surviving and other re-added BSSes (an order key per
BSS, so a configuration file reload still finds the file's order
whatever came back first), the way "ADD bss_config=" adds a BSS, with
hostapd_setup_bss(first = 0) so that, unlike the -1 of that command,
the link is added to the driver and to the AP MLD, under its previous
link ID when the AP MLD has not reused it, and under the link address
it had or the one its configuration names, never an automatic one: if
another live BSS holds that address the BSS stays parked and the
conflict is logged, so that two links never share an address. The AP
MLD must be the one the
BSS belonged to: the controller names an AP MLD after its primary VAP
and may create another network under that name, so the returning first
BSS's MLD address has to match the one recorded or the one the parked
configuration names, and a parked BSS whose AP MLD does not come back
within 60 s expires; both are logged. The re-add counts as done only
once the link add and the BSS setup succeeded; otherwise the BSS stays
parked. The new BSS borrows its driver context inside
hostapd_setup_bss() only, after its checks, so that a re-add that fails
before that (control socket, rejected address) cannot remove a link of
the containing interface's own AP MLD on the way out. So a REMOVE/ADD of the
owner alone, with the same AP MLD, restores all of its partners without
any controller action, and moving one AP out of and back into an AP MLD
leaves the other AP MLDs with all of their links (pWHM removes and
re-adds the radio whose VAP changes; its guest and backhaul links on the
other radios were lost before).

A partner supplied again meanwhile is not duplicated: once an ADD is
accepted for an interface on the same phy with a BSS of the same AP
MLD, or with a BSS with the same link address on any phy, the parked
copy is dropped, also when the controller gets a separate hostapd_iface
for it because its configuration starts with an AP MLD link. A
configuration file that is parsed and accepted for the interface
(RELOAD_CONFIG) is its complete set of BSSes and drops the parked BSSes
it omits or lists again. An in-memory RELOAD or RELOAD_BSS restates the
live BSSes and says nothing about the parked ones, which stay; pWHM
issues such reloads for unrelated parameter changes, and they must not
forfeit the links. A failed reload leaves the parked state alone.

An explicit DISABLE of the interface, including one that is already
down, or a REMOVE of the interface cancels its pending recovery. A
parked BSS is addressed by the control socket name it had: "REMOVE
<mld>_link<N>" drops exactly that one, and a bare "REMOVE <mld>" drops
the parked BSS of that AP MLD if there is exactly one. Every live
interface, BSS and control socket name and every parked BSS the name
matches is resolved before anything is removed: a name that denotes
both a live object and a parked BSS, or several parked BSSes, removes
nothing and fails with a log line, since the name shared by the links
of an AP MLD does not say which radio is meant. A name that matches no
parked BSS is handled as before. pWHM removes an interface by its first
BSS's socket name after "SET interface", which meets a parked BSS only
if that AP MLD gave the same link ID to a live link on another radio
while the parked one waits; that REMOVE then fails and pWHM falls back
to its restart. No memory of names is kept after a parked BSS is gone,
so a REMOVE that arrives after the re-add or the cancellation acts on
whatever carries the name then. The recovery timer is cancelled once
nothing is pending anywhere. The eviction itself uses an internal
disable that does not cancel the recovery.

Limits left to the controller: a parked BSS is the configuration the
link had, so a network changed meanwhile under the same AP MLD address
(SSID, credentials) comes back with the old configuration until the
controller re-applies it, which a REMOVE/ADD or an accepted
configuration file does, and nothing is re-added after the 60 s bound;
names are not remembered once a parked BSS was re-added, removed or
expired, so a later REMOVE acts on whatever live object carries the
name then, as before; a failed kernel link removal is not reconciled,
the link ID is reused when hostapd knows no BSS holding it, and a stale
kernel link makes the re-add fail until the BSS expires.

If the owner comes back as a plain BSS, or with another AP MLD, the
partners' configurations no longer describe a link that can exist: they
stay down or parked until the controller re-applies them. pWHM does so
in the flows that cause such a re-ADD, since the change of the primary
link marks the configured neighbour links for an AP MLD configuration
refresh; a REMOVE of the partner interface then drops its parked BSSes.

For a plain owner the borrower selection, the teardown order, the
first-BSS partner handling, hostapd_remove_bss() and
hostapd_cleanup_driver() are unchanged; the configuration of a
secondary AP MLD link partner is now retained and its recovery is
pending instead of the partner being lost.

Signed-off-by: Petr Štetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
---
 src/ap/hostapd.c | 868 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 src/ap/hostapd.h |  37 ++
 2 files changed, 898 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/ap/hostapd.c b/src/ap/hostapd.c
index d4e66426e2f5..c1e5aa6486d0 100644
--- a/src/ap/hostapd.c
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.c
@@ -70,6 +70,16 @@ static void hostapd_cleanup_unused_mlds(struct hapd_interfaces *interfaces);
 static int hostapd_remove_bss(struct hostapd_iface *iface, unsigned int idx);
 static void hostapd_interface_setup_failure_handler(void *eloop_ctx,
 						    void *timeout_ctx);
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+static void hostapd_mld_reattach_partners(void *eloop_ctx, void *timeout_ctx);
+static bool hostapd_mld_recovery_pending(struct hapd_interfaces *interfaces);
+static void hostapd_mld_revoke_recovery(struct hostapd_iface *iface);
+static void hostapd_mld_drop_parked_bss(struct hostapd_iface *iface,
+					const char *reason);
+static void hostapd_mld_drop_resupplied_parked_bss(struct hostapd_iface *iface);
+static void hostapd_mld_reconcile_parked_bss(struct hostapd_iface *iface);
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
+static int hostapd_disable_iface_int(struct hostapd_iface *hapd_iface);
 #ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211AX
 static void hostapd_switch_color_timeout_handler(void *eloop_data,
 						 void *user_ctx);
@@ -373,6 +383,10 @@ int hostapd_reload_config(struct hostapd_iface *iface)
 	}
 
 	hostapd_config_free(oldconf);
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+	/* The file is the complete accepted set of BSSes of this interface */
+	hostapd_mld_reconcile_parked_bss(iface);
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 
 
 	return 0;
@@ -2830,6 +2844,24 @@ dfs_offload:
 	if (iface->interfaces && iface->interfaces->count > 1)
 		ieee802_11_set_beacons(iface);
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+	if (iface->interfaces) {
+		/* A BSS this interface runs replaces a parked copy of it */
+		hostapd_mld_drop_resupplied_parked_bss(iface);
+		/* This interface may have given an AP MLD a first BSS with a
+		 * driver again; let the partners
+		 * hostapd_remove_drv_borrowers() took down borrow it. Do it
+		 * from the event loop, outside of this setup. */
+		if (hostapd_mld_recovery_pending(iface->interfaces)) {
+			eloop_cancel_timeout(hostapd_mld_reattach_partners,
+					     iface->interfaces, NULL);
+			eloop_register_timeout(0, 0,
+					       hostapd_mld_reattach_partners,
+					       iface->interfaces, NULL);
+		}
+	}
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
+
 	return 0;
 
 fail:
@@ -3126,6 +3158,7 @@ void hostapd_interface_free(struct hostapd_iface *iface)
 	size_t j;
 	wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "%s(%p)", __func__, iface);
 #ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+	hostapd_mld_drop_parked_bss(iface, "interface freed");
 	/* A BSS elsewhere that still names this interface as the owner of its
 	 * driver runs on a driver that was left alive by
 	 * hostapd_cleanup_driver(); nobody owns that driver any more. */
@@ -3546,6 +3579,763 @@ hostapd_interface_init_bss(struct hapd_interfaces *interfaces, const char *phy,
 }
 
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+
+/* How long a parked BSS waits for a first BSS of its AP MLD (seconds); a
+ * pWHM warm re-add of the owner radio takes about two seconds. */
+#define HOSTAPD_MLD_PARKED_BSS_TIMEOUT 60
+
+static void hostapd_mld_parked_bss_expire(void *eloop_ctx, void *timeout_ctx);
+
+
+static bool hostapd_mld_recovery_pending(struct hapd_interfaces *interfaces)
+{
+	size_t i;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < interfaces->count; i++) {
+		struct hostapd_iface *iface = interfaces->iface[i];
+
+		if (iface && (iface->mld_partner_disabled ||
+			      iface->num_mld_parked_bss))
+			return true;
+	}
+
+	return false;
+}
+
+
+/* Release the parked array and the expiry timer once the list is empty, and
+ * the recovery timer once nothing is pending anywhere. */
+static void hostapd_mld_parked_bss_changed(struct hostapd_iface *iface)
+{
+	if (iface->num_mld_parked_bss)
+		return;
+	os_free(iface->mld_parked_bss);
+	iface->mld_parked_bss = NULL;
+	eloop_cancel_timeout(hostapd_mld_parked_bss_expire, iface, NULL);
+	if (iface->interfaces &&
+	    !hostapd_mld_recovery_pending(iface->interfaces))
+		eloop_cancel_timeout(hostapd_mld_reattach_partners,
+				     iface->interfaces, NULL);
+}
+
+
+/* Forget parked BSS idx of iface and free its configuration. */
+static void hostapd_mld_drop_parked_bss_idx(struct hostapd_iface *iface,
+					    size_t idx, const char *reason)
+{
+	struct hostapd_mld_parked_bss *p = &iface->mld_parked_bss[idx];
+	size_t i;
+
+	wpa_printf(MSG_INFO,
+		   "Drop parked BSS '%s' (AP MLD link %u, BSSID " MACSTR
+		   ") of phy %s: %s",
+		   p->conf->iface, p->link_id, MAC2STR(p->bssid), iface->phy,
+		   reason);
+	hostapd_config_free_bss(p->conf);
+	iface->num_mld_parked_bss--;
+	for (i = idx; i < iface->num_mld_parked_bss; i++)
+		iface->mld_parked_bss[i] = iface->mld_parked_bss[i + 1];
+	hostapd_mld_parked_bss_changed(iface);
+}
+
+
+static void hostapd_mld_drop_parked_bss(struct hostapd_iface *iface,
+					const char *reason)
+{
+	while (iface->num_mld_parked_bss)
+		hostapd_mld_drop_parked_bss_idx(
+			iface, iface->num_mld_parked_bss - 1, reason);
+}
+
+
+/* Run the expiry timer of iface at the earliest expiry of its parked BSSes */
+static void hostapd_mld_parked_bss_arm_expiry(struct hostapd_iface *iface)
+{
+	struct os_reltime now, first, delay;
+	size_t i;
+
+	eloop_cancel_timeout(hostapd_mld_parked_bss_expire, iface, NULL);
+	if (!iface->num_mld_parked_bss)
+		return;
+	first = iface->mld_parked_bss[0].expiry;
+	for (i = 1; i < iface->num_mld_parked_bss; i++) {
+		if (os_reltime_before(&iface->mld_parked_bss[i].expiry, &first))
+			first = iface->mld_parked_bss[i].expiry;
+	}
+	os_get_reltime(&now);
+	if (os_reltime_before(&first, &now))
+		delay.sec = delay.usec = 0;
+	else
+		os_reltime_sub(&first, &now, &delay);
+	eloop_register_timeout(delay.sec, delay.usec,
+			       hostapd_mld_parked_bss_expire, iface, NULL);
+}
+
+
+/* Keep a parked BSS record on iface. Frees the configuration if the record
+ * cannot be stored. */
+static void hostapd_mld_park_record(struct hostapd_iface *iface,
+				    const struct hostapd_mld_parked_bss *p)
+{
+	struct hostapd_mld_parked_bss *tmp;
+
+	tmp = os_realloc_array(iface->mld_parked_bss,
+			       iface->num_mld_parked_bss + 1, sizeof(*tmp));
+	if (!tmp) {
+		wpa_printf(MSG_WARNING,
+			   "Cannot park BSS '%s' (AP MLD link %u): out of memory, it is lost",
+			   p->conf->iface, p->link_id);
+		hostapd_config_free_bss(p->conf);
+		return;
+	}
+	iface->mld_parked_bss = tmp;
+	tmp[iface->num_mld_parked_bss++] = *p;
+	hostapd_mld_parked_bss_arm_expiry(iface);
+}
+
+
+/* A parked BSS whose AP MLD did not come back in time is dropped: the
+ * controller has moved on, and a copy of what the AP MLD was must not join
+ * whatever carries its name later. */
+static void hostapd_mld_parked_bss_expire(void *eloop_ctx, void *timeout_ctx)
+{
+	struct hostapd_iface *iface = eloop_ctx;
+	struct os_reltime now;
+	char reason[80];
+	size_t k;
+
+	os_get_reltime(&now);
+	os_snprintf(reason, sizeof(reason),
+		    "expired, not re-added within %d s",
+		    HOSTAPD_MLD_PARKED_BSS_TIMEOUT);
+	for (k = iface->num_mld_parked_bss; k > 0; k--) {
+		if (!os_reltime_before(&now, &iface->mld_parked_bss[k - 1].expiry))
+			hostapd_mld_drop_parked_bss_idx(iface, k - 1, reason);
+	}
+	if (iface->num_mld_parked_bss)
+		hostapd_mld_parked_bss_arm_expiry(iface);
+}
+
+
+/* An explicit disable or removal of the interface cancels its pending
+ * automatic recovery: it stays down, and its parked BSSes are forgotten. */
+static void hostapd_mld_revoke_recovery(struct hostapd_iface *iface)
+{
+	if (!iface->mld_partner_disabled && !iface->num_mld_parked_bss)
+		return;
+
+	wpa_printf(MSG_INFO,
+		   "Interface %s: cancel pending AP MLD partner recovery (%u parked BSS)",
+		   iface->phy, (unsigned int) iface->num_mld_parked_bss);
+	iface->mld_partner_disabled = 0;
+	hostapd_mld_drop_parked_bss(iface, "recovery cancelled");
+	if (iface->interfaces &&
+	    !hostapd_mld_recovery_pending(iface->interfaces))
+		eloop_cancel_timeout(hostapd_mld_reattach_partners,
+				     iface->interfaces, NULL);
+}
+
+
+/* Take down secondary BSS idx of iface the way hostapd_remove_bss() does,
+ * but keep its configuration, with the identity the BSS had, for
+ * hostapd_mld_reattach_partners(). */
+static void hostapd_mld_park_bss(struct hostapd_iface *iface, unsigned int idx,
+				 struct hostapd_iface *owner)
+{
+	struct hostapd_data *hapd = iface->bss[idx];
+	struct hostapd_mld_parked_bss p;
+	size_t i;
+
+	/* Order keys: assigned to all BSSes of the interface the first time
+	 * one of them is parked (their positions then), and to a BSS added
+	 * later, without a key, after every existing live and parked one.
+	 * A re-added BSS is inserted by this key, so that the interface keeps
+	 * the order of its configuration file however many BSSes are parked
+	 * and in whatever order they come back. */
+	if (!iface->num_mld_parked_bss) {
+		bool keyed = false;
+
+		for (i = 0; i < iface->num_bss; i++)
+			keyed |= iface->bss[i]->mld_bss_order != 0;
+		if (!keyed) {
+			for (i = 0; i < iface->num_bss; i++)
+				iface->bss[i]->mld_bss_order = i + 1;
+		}
+	}
+	if (!hapd->mld_bss_order) {
+		unsigned int max = 0;
+
+		for (i = 0; i < iface->num_bss; i++) {
+			if (iface->bss[i]->mld_bss_order > max)
+				max = iface->bss[i]->mld_bss_order;
+		}
+		for (i = 0; i < iface->num_mld_parked_bss; i++) {
+			if (iface->mld_parked_bss[i].order > max)
+				max = iface->mld_parked_bss[i].order;
+		}
+		hapd->mld_bss_order = max + 1;
+	}
+
+	os_memset(&p, 0, sizeof(p));
+	p.conf = hapd->conf;
+	p.link_id = hapd->mld_link_id;
+	p.order = hapd->mld_bss_order;
+	os_memcpy(p.bssid, hapd->own_addr, ETH_ALEN);
+	if (hapd->mld)
+		os_memcpy(p.mld_addr, hapd->mld->mld_addr, ETH_ALEN);
+	os_get_reltime(&p.expiry);
+	p.expiry.sec += HOSTAPD_MLD_PARKED_BSS_TIMEOUT;
+
+	wpa_printf(MSG_INFO,
+		   "Park BSS '%s' (AP MLD link %u, BSSID " MACSTR
+		   ") of interface %s: it uses the driver of %s that is being deinitialized",
+		   hapd->conf->iface, hapd->mld_link_id,
+		   MAC2STR(hapd->own_addr), iface->bss[0]->conf->iface,
+		   owner->bss[0]->conf->iface);
+
+	/* As hostapd_remove_bss(), without hostapd_config_free_bss() */
+	hostapd_bss_deinit(hapd);
+	hapd->conf = NULL;
+	hostapd_mld_ref_dec(hapd->mld);
+	os_free(hapd);
+
+	iface->num_bss--;
+	for (i = idx; i < iface->num_bss; i++)
+		iface->bss[i] = iface->bss[i + 1];
+	iface->conf->num_bss--;
+	for (i = idx; i < iface->conf->num_bss; i++)
+		iface->conf->bss[i] = iface->conf->bss[i + 1];
+
+	hostapd_mld_park_record(iface, &p);
+}
+
+
+static struct hostapd_data *
+hostapd_mld_running_first_bss(struct hapd_interfaces *interfaces,
+			      const char *mld_name)
+{
+	size_t i;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < interfaces->mld_count; i++) {
+		struct hostapd_mld *mld = interfaces->mld[i];
+
+		if (mld && os_strcmp(mld->name, mld_name) == 0 && mld->fbss &&
+		    mld->fbss->drv_priv &&
+		    mld->fbss->iface->state == HAPD_IFACE_ENABLED)
+			return mld->fbss;
+	}
+
+	return NULL;
+}
+
+
+/* Whether the AP MLD that fbss now starts is the one parked BSS p belonged
+ * to: the MLD address it had, or the one its configuration names. The name
+ * alone is not enough, the controller names an AP MLD after its primary VAP
+ * and may create a different network under it. */
+static bool hostapd_mld_parked_bss_mld_ok(const struct hostapd_mld_parked_bss *p,
+					  struct hostapd_data *fbss)
+{
+	const u8 *addr = fbss->mld ? fbss->mld->mld_addr : NULL;
+
+	if (!addr || is_zero_ether_addr(addr))
+		return false;
+	if (is_zero_ether_addr(p->mld_addr) &&
+	    is_zero_ether_addr(p->conf->mld_addr))
+		return true;
+	return ether_addr_equal(addr, p->mld_addr) ||
+		ether_addr_equal(addr, p->conf->mld_addr);
+}
+
+
+static bool hostapd_mld_link_id_in_use(struct hapd_interfaces *interfaces,
+				       struct hostapd_mld *mld, u8 link_id)
+{
+	size_t i, j;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < interfaces->count; i++) {
+		struct hostapd_iface *iface = interfaces->iface[i];
+
+		for (j = 0; iface && j < iface->num_bss; j++) {
+			if (iface->bss[j]->mld == mld &&
+			    iface->bss[j]->mld_link_id == link_id)
+				return true;
+		}
+	}
+
+	return false;
+}
+
+
+/* The live BSS other than self whose link address, in use or configured, is
+ * addr; NULL if there is none. */
+static struct hostapd_data *
+hostapd_mld_addr_holder(struct hapd_interfaces *interfaces, const u8 *addr,
+			struct hostapd_data *self)
+{
+	size_t i, j;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < interfaces->count; i++) {
+		struct hostapd_iface *iface = interfaces->iface[i];
+
+		for (j = 0; iface && j < iface->num_bss; j++) {
+			struct hostapd_data *hapd = iface->bss[j];
+
+			if (hapd != self &&
+			    (ether_addr_equal(hapd->own_addr, addr) ||
+			     ether_addr_equal(hapd->conf->bssid, addr)))
+				return hapd;
+		}
+	}
+
+	return NULL;
+}
+
+
+/* Whether a live BSS describes the same link as parked BSS p of iface: the
+ * same AP MLD on the same phy, or the same link address. The controller may
+ * have supplied it again to any interface of the phy, including a separate
+ * interface it gets when its configuration starts with an AP MLD link. */
+static bool hostapd_mld_parked_bss_is_live(struct hapd_interfaces *interfaces,
+					   struct hostapd_iface *iface,
+					   const struct hostapd_mld_parked_bss *p)
+{
+	size_t i, j;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < interfaces->count; i++) {
+		struct hostapd_iface *other = interfaces->iface[i];
+
+		for (j = 0; other && j < other->num_bss; j++) {
+			struct hostapd_data *hapd = other->bss[j];
+
+			if (!hapd->conf->mld_ap)
+				continue;
+			if (os_strcmp(other->phy, iface->phy) == 0 &&
+			    os_strcmp(hapd->conf->iface, p->conf->iface) == 0)
+				return true;
+			if (!is_zero_ether_addr(p->bssid) &&
+			    (ether_addr_equal(hapd->own_addr, p->bssid) ||
+			     ether_addr_equal(hapd->conf->bssid, p->bssid)))
+				return true;
+		}
+	}
+
+	return false;
+}
+
+
+/* A BSS supplied again while its previous instance is parked replaces the
+ * parked copy. Called once an interface has set up its BSSes. */
+static void hostapd_mld_drop_resupplied_parked_bss(struct hostapd_iface *iface)
+{
+	struct hapd_interfaces *interfaces = iface->interfaces;
+	size_t i, k;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < interfaces->count; i++) {
+		struct hostapd_iface *other = interfaces->iface[i];
+
+		if (!other)
+			continue;
+		for (k = other->num_mld_parked_bss; k > 0; k--) {
+			if (hostapd_mld_parked_bss_is_live(
+				    interfaces, other,
+				    &other->mld_parked_bss[k - 1]))
+				hostapd_mld_drop_parked_bss_idx(
+					other, k - 1, "supplied again");
+		}
+	}
+}
+
+
+/* Reconcile the parked BSSes of iface with a configuration file that was
+ * parsed and accepted for it: the file is its complete set of BSSes, so a
+ * parked BSS it lists is a duplicate of a live one and a parked BSS it omits
+ * was deleted by the controller. Only a file says that; an in-memory RELOAD
+ * or RELOAD_BSS restates the live BSSes and leaves the parked ones alone. */
+static void hostapd_mld_reconcile_parked_bss(struct hostapd_iface *iface)
+{
+	size_t j, k;
+
+	for (k = iface->num_mld_parked_bss; k > 0; k--) {
+		struct hostapd_mld_parked_bss *p = &iface->mld_parked_bss[k - 1];
+		bool listed = false;
+
+		for (j = 0; j < iface->conf->num_bss; j++) {
+			if (os_strcmp(iface->conf->bss[j]->iface,
+				      p->conf->iface) == 0)
+				listed = true;
+		}
+		hostapd_mld_drop_parked_bss_idx(
+			iface, k - 1, listed ? "configured again" :
+			"not in the reloaded configuration file");
+	}
+}
+
+
+/* Parse "<mld>_link<N>" into <mld> and N; returns N, or -1 for a bare name. */
+static int hostapd_mld_parse_link_sock_name(const char *buf, char *name,
+					    size_t name_len)
+{
+	const char *pos = NULL, *q = buf;
+	char *end;
+	long id;
+
+	while ((q = os_strstr(q, "_" WPA_CTRL_IFACE_LINK_NAME)))
+		pos = q++;
+	if (!pos || pos == buf || (size_t) (pos - buf) >= name_len)
+		return -1;
+	q = pos + 1 + os_strlen(WPA_CTRL_IFACE_LINK_NAME);
+	if (*q < '0' || *q > '9')
+		return -1;
+	id = strtol(q, &end, 10);
+	if (*end || id < 0 || id >= MAX_NUM_MLD_LINKS)
+		return -1;
+	os_memcpy(name, buf, pos - buf);
+	name[pos - buf] = '\0';
+	return (int) id;
+}
+
+
+/* Resolve a REMOVE name against the parked BSSes before anything is removed.
+ * "REMOVE <mld>_link<N>", the control socket name the BSS had, means the
+ * parked BSS that was link N of AP MLD <mld>; a bare "REMOVE <mld>" means
+ * the parked BSS of that AP MLD if there is exactly one. Returns 0 with
+ * *handled set when that parked BSS was dropped, -1 with *handled set when
+ * the name matches a parked BSS but also a live interface, BSS or control
+ * socket name or several parked BSSes (nothing is removed then: a name that
+ * denotes two objects removes neither), and -1 with *handled clear when no
+ * parked BSS matches, so that the live objects are searched as before. */
+static int hostapd_mld_remove_parked_bss(struct hapd_interfaces *interfaces,
+					 const char *buf, bool *handled)
+{
+	struct hostapd_iface *match_iface = NULL;
+	char name[IFNAMSIZ + 1];
+	int link_id, parked = 0, live = 0;
+	size_t i, j, k, match_idx = 0;
+
+	*handled = false;
+	link_id = hostapd_mld_parse_link_sock_name(buf, name, sizeof(name));
+
+	for (i = 0; i < interfaces->count; i++) {
+		struct hostapd_iface *iface = interfaces->iface[i];
+
+		if (!iface)
+			continue;
+		for (k = iface->num_mld_parked_bss; k > 0; k--) {
+			struct hostapd_mld_parked_bss *p =
+				&iface->mld_parked_bss[k - 1];
+
+			if (link_id >= 0 ? (p->link_id != link_id ||
+					    os_strcmp(p->conf->iface, name)) :
+			    os_strcmp(p->conf->iface, buf))
+				continue;
+			parked++;
+			match_iface = iface;
+			match_idx = k - 1;
+		}
+	}
+	if (!parked)
+		return -1;
+	*handled = true;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < interfaces->count; i++) {
+		struct hostapd_iface *iface = interfaces->iface[i];
+
+		if (!iface)
+			continue;
+		if (os_strcmp(iface->phy, buf) == 0)
+			live++;
+		for (j = 0; j < iface->conf->num_bss; j++) {
+			if (os_strcmp(iface->conf->bss[j]->iface, buf) == 0)
+				live++;
+		}
+		for (j = 0; j < iface->num_bss; j++) {
+			if (iface->bss[j]->conf->mld_ap &&
+			    os_strcmp(iface->bss[j]->ctrl_sock_iface, buf) == 0)
+				live++;
+		}
+	}
+
+	if (live || parked != 1) {
+		wpa_printf(MSG_INFO,
+			   "Remove '%s': ambiguous, %d parked BSS and %d live interface/BSS/control socket match it; nothing removed, use REMOVE <mld>_%s<N> or remove the interface",
+			   buf, parked, live, WPA_CTRL_IFACE_LINK_NAME);
+		return -1;
+	}
+
+	wpa_printf(MSG_INFO, "Remove parked BSS '%s'", buf);
+	hostapd_mld_drop_parked_bss_idx(match_iface, match_idx, "REMOVE");
+	return 0;
+}
+
+
+/* Add parked BSS p back to its running interface the way "ADD bss_config="
+ * adds a BSS to an existing interface, as a non-first link of its AP MLD
+ * whose running first BSS is fbss. Returns 0 once the link was added to the
+ * driver and the BSS set up; p->conf then belongs to iface. Otherwise the BSS
+ * is not added, p->conf is untouched and -1 is returned. */
+static int hostapd_mld_unpark_bss(struct hostapd_iface *iface,
+				  const struct hostapd_mld_parked_bss *p,
+				  struct hostapd_data *fbss)
+{
+	struct hostapd_bss_config *conf = p->conf;
+	struct hostapd_bss_config **tmp_conf;
+	struct hostapd_data **tmp_bss, *hapd, *holder;
+	struct hostapd_mld *mld;
+	const u8 *addr;
+	size_t i, pos;
+
+	tmp_conf = os_realloc_array(iface->conf->bss, iface->conf->num_bss + 1,
+				    sizeof(*tmp_conf));
+	if (tmp_conf)
+		iface->conf->bss = tmp_conf;
+	tmp_bss = os_realloc_array(iface->bss, iface->num_bss + 1,
+				   sizeof(*tmp_bss));
+	if (tmp_bss)
+		iface->bss = tmp_bss;
+	if (!tmp_conf || !tmp_bss || iface->num_bss != iface->conf->num_bss)
+		return -1;
+
+	hapd = hostapd_alloc_bss_data(iface, iface->conf, conf);
+	if (!hapd)
+		return -1;
+
+	/* Back in its place by order key: before the first BSS that came
+	 * after it or has no key (added later), never before the first BSS,
+	 * so that a configuration file reload still finds the BSSes in the
+	 * file's order whatever came back first. */
+	hapd->mld_bss_order = p->order;
+	for (pos = 1; pos < iface->num_bss; pos++) {
+		if (!iface->bss[pos]->mld_bss_order ||
+		    iface->bss[pos]->mld_bss_order > p->order)
+			break;
+	}
+	for (i = iface->num_bss; i > pos; i--) {
+		iface->bss[i] = iface->bss[i - 1];
+		iface->conf->bss[i] = iface->conf->bss[i - 1];
+	}
+	iface->bss[pos] = hapd;
+	iface->conf->bss[pos] = conf;
+	iface->num_bss++;
+	iface->conf->num_bss++;
+
+	hapd->msg_ctx = hapd;
+	hostapd_bss_setup_multi_link(hapd, iface->interfaces);
+	mld = hapd->mld;
+	if (!mld || hostapd_mld_get_first_bss(hapd) != fbss) {
+		wpa_printf(MSG_WARNING,
+			   "Cannot re-add BSS '%s': it did not join the AP MLD of %s",
+			   conf->iface, fbss->conf->iface);
+		goto fail;
+	}
+
+	/* Keep the link ID the BSS had, so that it comes back under its
+	 * previous control socket name, unless the AP MLD reused it. */
+	if (p->link_id < MAX_NUM_MLD_LINKS &&
+	    !hostapd_mld_link_id_in_use(iface->interfaces, mld, p->link_id)) {
+		if (mld->next_link_id == hapd->mld_link_id + 1)
+			mld->next_link_id--;
+		hapd->mld_link_id = p->link_id;
+		if (mld->next_link_id <= p->link_id)
+			mld->next_link_id = p->link_id + 1;
+	}
+
+	/* The link comes back under the address it had, or the one its
+	 * configuration names, and never under an automatic one: that would
+	 * be derived from the first BSS again, the same for every BSS re-added
+	 * here. If another live BSS holds that address now the BSS stays
+	 * parked, to be retried on the next interface setup until it expires;
+	 * two links never share an address. Checked on every attempt, also
+	 * for an address made explicit by an earlier one. */
+	addr = is_zero_ether_addr(conf->bssid) ? p->bssid : conf->bssid;
+	if (is_zero_ether_addr(addr)) {
+		wpa_printf(MSG_WARNING,
+			   "Cannot re-add BSS '%s' (AP MLD link %u) to interface %s: no link address recorded; it stays parked",
+			   conf->iface, hapd->mld_link_id,
+			   iface->bss[0]->conf->iface);
+		goto fail;
+	}
+	holder = hostapd_mld_addr_holder(iface->interfaces, addr, hapd);
+	if (holder) {
+		wpa_printf(MSG_WARNING,
+			   "Cannot re-add BSS '%s' (AP MLD link %u) to interface %s: its link address "
+			   MACSTR " is used by BSS '%s'; it stays parked",
+			   conf->iface, hapd->mld_link_id,
+			   iface->bss[0]->conf->iface, MAC2STR(addr),
+			   holder->conf->iface);
+		goto fail;
+	}
+	if (is_zero_ether_addr(conf->bssid))
+		os_memcpy(conf->bssid, addr, ETH_ALEN);
+
+	/* Only the driver operations and the base address for an automatic
+	 * link address; the driver context is borrowed from fbss by
+	 * hostapd_setup_bss() once the BSS passed its checks, so that a BSS
+	 * that fails before that has no context through which the unwind
+	 * could remove a link of the containing interface's own AP MLD. */
+	hapd->driver = iface->bss[0]->driver;
+	os_memcpy(hapd->own_addr, iface->bss[0]->own_addr, ETH_ALEN);
+
+	wpa_printf(MSG_INFO,
+		   "Re-add BSS '%s' (AP MLD link %u) to interface %s: its AP MLD has a first BSS with a driver again",
+		   conf->iface, hapd->mld_link_id, iface->bss[0]->conf->iface);
+	/* first = 0: a non-first BSS of the interface. hostapd_setup_bss()
+	 * makes it borrow the driver context of the first BSS of its AP MLD
+	 * and, unlike the -1 of "ADD bss_config=", adds the link to the driver
+	 * and to the AP MLD. */
+	if (start_ctrl_iface_bss(hapd) < 0 || hostapd_setup_bss(hapd, 0, true)) {
+		wpa_printf(MSG_WARNING,
+			   "Failed to re-add BSS '%s' (AP MLD link %u) to interface %s: it stays parked",
+			   conf->iface, hapd->mld_link_id,
+			   iface->bss[0]->conf->iface);
+		goto fail;
+	}
+	wpa_printf(MSG_INFO, "Re-added BSS '%s' as AP MLD link %u of interface %s",
+		   conf->iface, hapd->mld_link_id, iface->bss[0]->conf->iface);
+	hostapd_owe_update_trans(iface);
+	return 0;
+
+fail:
+	/* A link that was added is removed through the borrowed context; a
+	 * BSS that never borrowed one (control socket failure, rejected
+	 * address) has drv_priv NULL and hostapd_free_hapd_data() removes
+	 * nothing. */
+	hostapd_bss_link_deinit(hapd);
+	hostapd_cleanup(hapd);
+	iface->num_bss--;
+	iface->conf->num_bss--;
+	for (i = pos; i < iface->num_bss; i++) {
+		iface->bss[i] = iface->bss[i + 1];
+		iface->conf->bss[i] = iface->conf->bss[i + 1];
+	}
+	iface->bss[iface->num_bss] = NULL;
+	iface->conf->bss[iface->conf->num_bss] = NULL;
+	hapd->conf = NULL;
+	hostapd_mld_ref_dec(hapd->mld);
+	os_free(hapd);
+	return -1;
+}
+
+
+/**
+ * hostapd_mld_reattach_partners - Bring back the AP MLD partners taken down
+ * for a departed driver owner once their AP MLD has a first BSS again
+ * @eloop_ctx: struct hapd_interfaces *
+ * @timeout_ctx: Not used
+ *
+ * hostapd_remove_drv_borrowers() disables an interface whose first BSS is an
+ * AP MLD link borrowing the driver of an AP MLD owner interface that goes
+ * away (mld_partner_disabled) and parks the configuration of every secondary
+ * AP MLD link BSS that borrows the driver of an interface that goes away
+ * (mld_parked_bss). Once a first BSS of the same AP MLD runs again with a
+ * driver of its own, these can borrow that context as they did before: enable
+ * the interface, which runs driver_init() and the interface setup on its
+ * unchanged configuration, and add each parked BSS back to its still running
+ * interface, provided the AP MLD is the one it belonged to. A parked BSS
+ * whose re-add fails stays parked until its expiry. An explicit disable or
+ * removal revokes both (hostapd_mld_revoke_recovery()).
+ *
+ * Known limits, left to the controller:
+ * - A parked BSS is the configuration the link had. If the network changed
+ *   meanwhile under the same AP MLD address (SSID, credentials), the link
+ *   comes back with the old configuration until the controller re-applies
+ *   it; a REMOVE/ADD or an accepted configuration file replaces the parked
+ *   copy, and nothing is re-added after HOSTAPD_MLD_PARKED_BSS_TIMEOUT.
+ * - Names are not remembered once a parked BSS was re-added, removed or
+ *   expired: a REMOVE that arrives later acts on whatever live object
+ *   carries the name then, as it did before this change.
+ * - A failed kernel link removal is not reconciled: the link ID is reused
+ *   when hostapd knows no BSS holding it, and a stale kernel link makes the
+ *   re-add fail until the BSS expires.
+ */
+static void hostapd_mld_reattach_partners(void *eloop_ctx, void *timeout_ctx)
+{
+	struct hapd_interfaces *interfaces = eloop_ctx;
+	struct os_reltime now;
+	size_t i, k;
+
+	os_get_reltime(&now);
+
+	for (i = 0; i < interfaces->count; i++) {
+		struct hostapd_iface *iface = interfaces->iface[i];
+		struct hostapd_data *hapd;
+
+		if (!iface || !iface->num_bss)
+			continue;
+		hapd = iface->bss[0];
+
+		if (iface->mld_partner_disabled) {
+			if (iface->state != HAPD_IFACE_DISABLED ||
+			    hapd->drv_priv || !hapd->conf->mld_ap) {
+				/* Enabled meanwhile: nothing to do */
+				iface->mld_partner_disabled = 0;
+			} else if (hostapd_mld_running_first_bss(
+					   interfaces, hapd->conf->iface)) {
+				wpa_printf(MSG_INFO,
+					   "Re-enable interface %s: the AP MLD it borrows its driver from has a first BSS again",
+					   hapd->conf->iface);
+				iface->mld_partner_disabled = 0;
+				if (hostapd_enable_iface(iface))
+					wpa_printf(MSG_WARNING,
+						   "Failed to re-enable interface %s",
+						   hapd->conf->iface);
+			}
+		}
+
+		/* Parked secondaries need their own interface running */
+		if (!iface->num_mld_parked_bss || !hapd->drv_priv ||
+		    iface->state != HAPD_IFACE_ENABLED)
+			continue;
+
+		for (k = iface->num_mld_parked_bss; k > 0; k--) {
+			struct hostapd_mld_parked_bss p =
+				iface->mld_parked_bss[k - 1];
+			struct hostapd_data *fbss;
+			char reason[80];
+			size_t m;
+
+			if (!os_reltime_before(&now, &p.expiry)) {
+				hostapd_mld_drop_parked_bss_idx(
+					iface, k - 1, "expired");
+				continue;
+			}
+			if (hostapd_mld_parked_bss_is_live(interfaces, iface,
+							   &p)) {
+				hostapd_mld_drop_parked_bss_idx(
+					iface, k - 1, "supplied again");
+				continue;
+			}
+			fbss = hostapd_mld_running_first_bss(interfaces,
+							     p.conf->iface);
+			if (!fbss)
+				continue;
+			if (!hostapd_mld_parked_bss_mld_ok(&p, fbss)) {
+				os_snprintf(reason, sizeof(reason),
+					    "its AP MLD came back with MLD address "
+					    MACSTR ", it had " MACSTR,
+					    MAC2STR(fbss->mld->mld_addr),
+					    MAC2STR(p.mld_addr));
+				hostapd_mld_drop_parked_bss_idx(iface, k - 1,
+								reason);
+				continue;
+			}
+
+			/* Off the list while it is added; it goes back to the
+			 * end of the list if that fails. */
+			iface->num_mld_parked_bss--;
+			for (m = k - 1; m < iface->num_mld_parked_bss; m++)
+				iface->mld_parked_bss[m] =
+					iface->mld_parked_bss[m + 1];
+			if (hostapd_mld_unpark_bss(iface, &p, fbss))
+				hostapd_mld_park_record(iface, &p);
+		}
+		hostapd_mld_parked_bss_changed(iface);
+	}
+}
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
