+ * disabled for an AP MLD owner is marked mld_partner_disabled, and the
+ * configuration of a secondary partner that is an AP MLD link is parked with
+ * the identity the BSS had (hostapd_mld_park_bss()), whether the first BSS of
+ * the departing interface is an AP MLD link or a plain BSS whose interface
+ * hosts the first links of other AP MLDs. hostapd_mld_reattach_partners()
+ * restores both once their own AP MLD has a first BSS with a driver again.
+ * Only an AP MLD link borrows a context itself (hostapd_setup_bss() and
+ * driver_init(), both for conf->mld_ap); a plain secondary created through a
+ * borrowing first BSS records the same owner, but its interface is disabled
+ * as a first-BSS partner before the secondary walk gets to it. A plain
